# gitjig: source-only
# .githooks/helpers/secret-patterns — the staged-secret scan's committed
# rule source (SPEC §3.3 secret staged-scan semantics; §3.6's worked
# application binds the egress scan to this same single source).
#
# Format contract: one pattern per line as id<TAB>ERE — tab-delimited
# because a pattern may carry spaces; blank lines and #-leading lines are
# ignored. IDs are lowercase-hyphen tokens (the ID is what a refusal
# record carries). Patterns are constrained to the POSIX-ERE / RegExp
# common subset: no backreferences or lookarounds, no backslash-letter
# classes, no POSIX bracket classes — explicit ranges only — so every
# committed line compiles for both readers (the tier-2 bash matcher and
# the egress consumer when its own cycle lands).
#
# Format extensions must be COMPATIBLE extensions only: additions a
# current reader ignores, never a reinterpretation of existing lines —
# this is what bounds version skew between shell versions reading one
# repository's file (SPEC §3.3's enumerated residuals).
private-key	-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----
aws-access-key-id	(A3T[A-Z0-9]|AKIA|ASIA)[A-Z0-9]{16}
github-token	gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36,}
bearer-token	[Aa]uthorization: *[Bb]earer +[A-Za-z0-9._~+/=-]{20,}
